  "id": "face-to-face-group",
  "term": "face-to-face group",
  "definition": "A face-to-face group is an in-person meeting of participants, such as experts, who give and discuss their judgments together. In this source, it refers to an in-person group elicitation procedure used to gather experts’ estimates and express them as distributions.",
